First: Did all the patches get installed without complaints, or did the
patch utility give some error messages about failed chunks?
Look for file names ending with .rej in any directories affected,
especially src.

If two or more patches affect the same source files, they may conflict so
that the patch utility may be unable to find the right place to insert the
last patch(es) if a previouslu applied patch changed the context in a
difficult place. 
In that case you need to check the .rej file(s) and edit those parts
manually. 
If you get no failed chunks but only offset warnings, they are
usually harmless and tell that the patch utility found what looks like the
right context, but not exactly in the same line numbers it expected. This
often happens when the previously installed patch added some lines before
the place the later patch changes.

If you got no failed chunks, the next thing to wonder is whether the bug
is in one of the patches or in the original source.. 
I'm not familiar with all the patches you mentioned beside mine.. What
does the botl_held patch do? If it affects applying items in your
inventory, it may also do something to light sources when you change
levels. And so may additional levels. The coloralchemy probably doesn't.

